      "title": "Consciousness & Computation",
      "gist": "Conscious AI assumes computation suffices for consciousness, and four arguments weaken that assumption: brains are not computers, other kinds of processes exist, life may matter, and simulation is not the real thing.",
      "question": "Computational functionalism — why is computation not enough for consciousness? (four arguments)",
